## If there are connection issues with the DB:

# First, confirm connection error (rather than mistake in your code) by using local connection string:
# MONGO_URI = "mongodb://localhost:27017/test"

# If that works but Mongo's conn. string doesn't, try the following:

# Error ('ECONNREFUSED'):

# can be alleviated by using the following 'standard string format', as per MongoDB docs:
# mongodb://[username:password@]host1[:port1][,...hostN[:portN]][/[defaultauthdb][?options]]

# @ https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/troubleshoot-connection/#std-label-atlas-connection-refused-srv 
# @ https://www.mongodb.com/docs/upcoming/reference/connection-string/std-label-connections-standard-connection-string-format

# Another way of doing this is going to your database on MongoDB.com, and getting a conn. string for Node driver 2.2.12 or later:
